  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5412",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to SK-MEL3, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The first pathway links Mollicellin N to A704, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and this compound further targets SK-MEL3. In contrast, another pathway connects Mollicellin N to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a compound that also targets SK-MEL3. A third pathway shows Mollicellin N targeting TE-9, which is similarly targeted by a compound leading to SK-MEL3. These findings collectively suggest that Mollicellin N may act through different molecular mechanisms, potentially influencing SK-MEL3 through distinct pathways. The evidence supports the idea that Mollicellin N could be a potential therapeutic agent for SK-MEL3, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
